    pr_ref:  # 872a
    description: ""  # 872a
    fields:  # 872a
      severity: "medium"  # 872a
      statement: "hypergumbo explain <symbol> groups all incoming edges under 'Called by (N)' header and all outgoing under 'Calls (N)' header, but lists each edge with its actual type in brackets. For Symbol.from_dict (method): 'Called by (19)' header but first entry is 'Symbol [contains]' — the containing class, not a caller. For Span (class): 'Calls (2)' header but both entries are '[contains]' (the class containing its methods, not calling them). For Span 'Called by (2028)' header: entries are '[instantiates]' (creation, not call). The header counts include semantically different edge types: contains (containment) + instantiates (creation) + references (read) + calls (invocation) are all summed and labeled as 'Called by'. A user asking 'what calls Span' sees the containment hierarchy and instantiations in the answer, not pure callers."  # 872a
      root_cause: "cli.py cmd_explain groups all in/out edges by direction not by semantic relationship. The section labels conflate 'edges pointing at this node' with 'invocations of this node'. Pass-17 finding KKKKKK and pass-18 AAAAAAA noted axis-mixing in meta fields; this finding is the analogous CLI-output presentation drift."  # 872a
